{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-41388","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73235","text":"Round 27 B1.2 — the layer B1 presumed and did not have"}]},{"id":"blk-41389","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73236","marks":["bold"],"text":"Pack:"},{"id":"spn-73237","text":" "},{"id":"spn-73238","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM_B12_REVIEW_PACK.tar.gz"},{"id":"spn-73239","text":". Extract anywhere, run "},{"id":"spn-73240","marks":["code"],"text":"./verify.sh"},{"id":"spn-73241","text":". This run: "},{"id":"spn-73242","marks":["bold"],"text":"24 attempted / 24 passed / 0 failed / 0 skipped."}]},{"id":"blk-41390","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73243","text":"You took interpretation B and you were right. B1 froze an architecture the compiler could not express, and you saw it before a line of B2 was written."}]},{"id":"blk-41391","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73244","text":"1. There was no target-AST layer, so a port had nowhere to live"}]},{"id":"blk-41392","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73245","text":"Confirmed: "},{"id":"spn-73246","marks":["code"],"text":"lower()"},{"id":"spn-73247","text":" built an ic32 "},{"id":"spn-73248","marks":["bold"],"text":"string"},{"id":"spn-73249","text":". A port could only have become "},{"id":"spn-73250","marks":["code"],"text":"$input_x"},{"id":"spn-73251","text":" — spelling as semantics, the defect the ruling forbids, reintroduced by the absence of the representation it presumes."}]},{"id":"blk-41393","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73252","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM-TARGET-TEMPLATE-v1"},{"id":"spn-73253","text":", minimal, exactly today's fragment, with its own content-bound encoding id:"}]},{"id":"blk-41394","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Template := church(n) | add(Template, Template) | port(source_name)"},{"id":"blk-41395","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73254","marks":["bold"],"text":"And I-4a is now structural rather than promised."},{"id":"spn-73255","text":" A template contains "},{"id":"spn-73256","marks":["bold"],"text":"no binder names and no dup labels"},{"id":"spn-73257","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-73258","marks":["code"],"text":"emit()"},{"id":"spn-73259","text":" invents both from its shape by the declared depth-first policy. Two emitters allocating "},{"id":"spn-73260","marks":["code"],"text":"_impl17"},{"id":"spn-73261","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-73262","marks":["code"],"text":"q93"},{"id":"spn-73263","text":" cannot differ in the template because "},{"id":"spn-73264","marks":["italic"],"text":"there is no field an allocation could occupy"},{"id":"spn-73265","text":". That is a better answer than asking the emitter to behave. "},{"id":"spn-73266","marks":["code"],"text":"emit()"},{"id":"spn-73267","text":" refuses a template still holding a port."}]},{"id":"blk-41396","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73268","text":"I took one liberty worth flagging: your sketch listed "},{"id":"spn-73269","marks":["code"],"text":"lam"},{"id":"spn-73270","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-73271","marks":["code"],"text":"app"},{"id":"spn-73272","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-73273","marks":["code"],"text":"dup"},{"id":"spn-73274","text":"/binders as template nodes. I kept "},{"id":"spn-73275","marks":["code"],"text":"church(n)"},{"id":"spn-73276","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-73277","marks":["code"],"text":"add(a,b)"},{"id":"spn-73278","text":" opaque and pushed "},{"id":"spn-73279","marks":["bold"],"text":"all"},{"id":"spn-73280","text":" allocation into "},{"id":"spn-73281","marks":["code"],"text":"emit()"},{"id":"spn-73282","text":", which is what makes \"no field an allocation could occupy\" literally true. The cost is that the template does not yet model target binders structurally, so a future fragment with real lambdas will need to extend the grammar rather than inherit it. Say if you would rather have the fuller AST now."}]},{"id":"blk-41397","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73283","text":"2. The regression, which is why doing this before B2 was safe"}]},{"id":"blk-41398","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"pre-B1.2   lower(add(2,3)).target_term    129 chars\npost-B1.2  emit(template)                 129 chars     BYTE-IDENTICAL"},{"id":"blk-41399","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73284","text":"Verified against the previous commit's "},{"id":"spn-73285","marks":["code"],"text":"lower()"},{"id":"spn-73286","text":", and on a nested fixture. Same six-frame film, same normal form, same value 5, refinement still FILM-EVIDENCED. Introducing the phase changed neither the executable term nor its outcome."}]},{"id":"blk-41400","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73287","text":"3. "},{"id":"spn-73288","marks":["code"],"text":"LoweringReceipt"},{"id":"spn-73289","text":" was still the pre-B1 relation"}]},{"id":"blk-41401","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73290","text":"You were right that it is load-bearing. It ends at "},{"id":"spn-73291","marks":["code"],"text":"target_template_sem_id"},{"id":"spn-73292","text":" now (receipt domain v2); a receipt ending at the term keeps asserting lowering produced the executable term, which the two-level ruling denies."}]},{"id":"blk-41402","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73293","text":"4. The hashed semantics were still incomplete — B1.1's own defect, one round later"}]},{"id":"blk-41403","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73294","marks":["code"],"text":"lowered_ops"},{"id":"spn-73295","text":" was "},{"id":"spn-73296","marks":["code"],"text":"[\"const\",\"add\"]"},{"id":"spn-73297","text":", so "},{"id":"spn-73298","marks":["bold"],"text":"B2 adding `input` would have moved `LOWERING_SEM_ID`"},{"id":"spn-73299","text":". Exactly your interpretation-B point. The whole fragment including "},{"id":"spn-73300","marks":["code"],"text":"input"},{"id":"spn-73301","text":" is in the semantics now with its rule frozen:"}]},{"id":"blk-41404","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"{op:\"input\", name:N}  →  {t:\"port\", source_name:N}      N carried through UNCHANGED"},{"id":"blk-41405","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73302","text":"and "},{"id":"spn-73303","marks":["code"],"text":"lower-input-not-implemented"},{"id":"spn-73304","text":" is an "},{"id":"spn-73305","marks":["bold"],"text":"operational"},{"id":"spn-73306","text":" refusal in "},{"id":"spn-73307","marks":["code"],"text":"LOWERING_STATUS"},{"id":"spn-73308","text":", not a semantic one. "},{"id":"spn-73309","marks":["bold"],"text":"Measured by simulating B2"},{"id":"spn-73310","text":" — deleting the refusal line so "},{"id":"spn-73311","marks":["code"],"text":"input"},{"id":"spn-73312","text":" lowers, "},{"id":"spn-73313","marks":["italic"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-73314","text":" flipping both lifecycle flags:"}]},{"id":"blk-41406","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"baseline                     lsem-d95ee1cbc0e8f37   isem-bf9434fc751a2fb\ninput lowering IMPLEMENTED   lsem-d95ee1cbc0e8f37   isem-bf9434fc751a2fb\n+ implemented: true          lsem-d95ee1cbc0e8f37   isem-bf9434fc751a2fb"},{"id":"blk-41407","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73315","text":"Neither moves. The B1.1 promise is now true rather than nearly true. And the simulated B2 produces the right template for your I-4c fixture:"}]},{"id":"blk-41408","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"x + (x + y)  →  {t:add, a:{t:port,x}, b:{t:add, a:{t:port,x}, b:{t:port,y}}}\nports [\"x\",\"y\"] · emit → emit-unbound-port: x"},{"id":"blk-41409","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73316","text":"5. "},{"id":"spn-73317","marks":["code"],"text":"consumed_inputs"},{"id":"spn-73318","text":", named so it cannot be erased"}]},{"id":"blk-41410","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73319","text":"Your grant-versus-footprint framing is in "},{"id":"spn-73320","marks":["code"],"text":"INSTANTIATION_SEMANTICS"},{"id":"spn-73321","text":". Supplied and consumed inputs are different sets, "},{"id":"spn-73322","marks":["code"],"text":"inputs_sem_id"},{"id":"spn-73323","text":" commits to the whole supplied record, and no "},{"id":"spn-73324","marks":["code"],"text":"input_footprint"},{"id":"spn-73325","text":" is emitted yet — named rather than implied, so B2 cannot collapse it by accident."}]},{"id":"blk-41411","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73326","text":"6. The stale header"}]},{"id":"blk-41412","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73327","text":"Fixed. It drew "},{"id":"spn-73328","marks":["code"],"text":"program_sem_id → target_term_sem_id"},{"id":"spn-73329","text":" and said the inputs model was undecided while the sections below said the opposite — a file contradicting itself, which is the class this tree does not tolerate anywhere else."}]},{"id":"blk-41413","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73330","text":"Gate"}]},{"id":"blk-41414","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-73331","text":"grid "},{"id":"spn-73332","marks":["bold"],"text":"v1.36.0"},{"id":"spn-73333","text":" — 77 entries / 372 citations · "},{"id":"spn-73334","marks":["code"],"text":"lowering.mjs"},{"id":"spn-73335","text":" "},{"id":"spn-73336","marks":["bold"],"text":"0.4.0"},{"id":"spn-73337","text":" · negative battery "},{"id":"spn-73338","marks":["bold"],"text":"221/221"},{"id":"spn-73339","text":" (six new B1.2 forgeries) · lowering "},{"id":"spn-73340","marks":["bold"],"text":"12/12"},{"id":"spn-73341","text":", refinement unchanged and still FILM-EVIDENCED · derive 45/45 · realm 24/24 · bridge 48/48 · film 16/16 · twelve paired probes · harness 9/9 · runner 3/3 · pack "},{"id":"spn-73342","marks":["bold"],"text":"24/24, 0 skipped"},{"id":"spn-73343","text":". "},{"id":"spn-73344","marks":["code"],"text":"cert_id a08ee15d…"},{"id":"spn-73345","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-73346","marks":["bold"],"text":"thirtieth"},{"id":"spn-73347","text":" consecutive round."}]},{"id":"blk-41415","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-73348","text":"B2 is now small"}]},{"id":"blk-41416","items":[{"blocks":